<title>UK: Lower prices fail to excite buyers on UK meals.</title>
<headline>Lower prices fail to excite buyers on UK meals.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Falls of as much as four stg a tonne in high protein soymeal prices failed to excite buyers on the UK meals and feeds market on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;We've seen some buying at this morning's line up prices, but there has not been a great deal of tonnage behind it.&quot; said one broker.</p>
<p>High protein soymeal traded at 219 stg a tonne ex-store east coast while 197 stg was paid for May.</p>
<p>--Jim Ballantyne, London Newsroom, +44 171 542 8062</p>
